  "content": {
    "id": "p140-q12-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "12",
    "prompt": "Let $f(x)=\\frac{1}{x}$.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p140-q12-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "State the domain of $f(f(x))$.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$(-\\infty,0)\\cup(0,\\infty)$.",
          "worked": "The inner reciprocal requires $x\\ne0$. For every such input, $f(x)=\\frac{1}{x}\\ne0$, so the outer reciprocal is also defined.\n\nThe domain is $(-\\infty,0)\\cup(0,\\infty)$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 12
      },
      {
        "id": "p140-q12-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "Sketch the graph of $y=f(f(x))$.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "The line $y=x$ for $x\\ne0$, with an open circle at $(0,0)$.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}f(f(x))&=f\\left(\\frac{1}{x}\\right)\\\\f(f(x))&=\\frac{1}{\\frac{1}{x}}\\\\f(f(x))&=x\\qquad(x\\ne0).\\end{align*}$$\n\nSketch the line $y=x$, passing through $(1,1)$. Leave an open circle at $(0,0)$ because the original composition is undefined there.",
          "solutionDiagrams": [
            {
              "id": "p140-q12-b-solution-graph",
              "role": "solution",
              "format": "tikz",
              "code": "% mathsmap-diagram-colours {\"version\":1,\"kind\":\"graph\",\"base\":[],\"semantic\":[{\"name\":\"seriesBlue\",\"hex\":\"268CFF\",\"reason\":\"Composite-function graph series and its associated point markers\"}],\"reference\":\"Teacher PDF 30, printed 608, Exercise 2O Q12(b)\"}\n\\begin{tikzpicture}[x=10mm,y=10mm,>=stealth,font=\\fontsize{10}{12}\\selectfont]\n\\definecolor{seriesBlue}{HTML}{268CFF}\n\\special{dvisvgm:raw <metadata data-graph-strokes=\"1\"/>}\n\\path[use as bounding box] (-2.6,-2.6) rectangle (2.9,2.9);\n\\draw[black,line width=0.5pt,->] (-2.45,0)--(2.45,0);\n\\draw[black,line width=0.5pt,->] (0,-2.45)--(0,2.45);\n\\draw[black,line width=0.4pt,dashed] (0,1)--(1,1)--(1,0);\n\\draw[seriesBlue,line width=0.8pt,<->] plot[domain=-2.25:2.25,samples=2] (\\x,{\\x});\n\\filldraw[draw=seriesBlue,fill=seriesBlue,line width=0.4pt] (1,1) circle[radius=1.2pt];\n\\filldraw[draw=seriesBlue,fill=white,line width=0.8pt] (0,0) circle[radius=1.6pt];\n\\node[black,anchor=north,yshift=-3pt] at (2.45,0) {$x$};\n\\node[black,anchor=south east,xshift=-2pt] at (0,2.45) {$y$};\n\\node[black,anchor=north,yshift=-2pt,font=\\fontsize{8.5}{10.2}\\selectfont] at (1,0) {\\special{dvisvgm:raw <g data-graph-text=\"tick\">}$1$\\special{dvisvgm:raw </g>}};\n\\node[black,anchor=east,xshift=-2pt,font=\\fontsize{8.5}{10.2}\\selectfont] at (0,1) {\\special{dvisvgm:raw <g data-graph-text=\"tick\">}$1$\\special{dvisvgm:raw </g>}};\n\\end{tikzpicture}",
              "src": null,
